# Force LF everywhere, regardless of platform checkout settings.
#
# Windows CI runners default to `core.autocrlf=true`, which converts LF to
# CRLF on checkout for anything Git considers text. That silently shifted
# every byte offset in `crates/lux-syntax/tests/fixtures/**/*` relative to
# the `.tokens` golden files (recorded in LF), breaking
# `cargo test -p lux-syntax --test golden_tokens` on `windows-latest` only
# -- invisible on macOS/Linux, where the stored blobs are already LF and
# stay LF on checkout. `Eol::detect`'s own default is LF (this project's
# style, see `crates/lux-core/src/buffer/eol.rs`); this just makes Git
# checkouts agree with that everywhere, not only what already-decoded
# buffer content defaults to.
* text=auto eol=lf
